    "updated_at": "2017-10-05T13:26:50Z",
    "body": "Chrome is doing this because it is dispatching a focus event directly as opposed to calling the focus method on the field. If it called focus() then yes the correct events would fire. Albeit that chrome fires the focusin/out & focus/blur in non-standard order already. \r\n\r\nI wonder if it was done this way because focusing a field causes it to scroll into view I believe which would be an under-desirable property of autofilling but I'd have to do more research.\r\n\r\n",
